    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm worried about the buffet specifically though. With 500 people moving through, things get messy fast. If a vegan dish accidentally gets a scoop from a non-vegan dish or vice versa, it's a disaster. \n\nDo you have any advice on how to physically layout the station or manage the serving utensils to prevent cross-contamination? Like, should we have separate stations or just be really strict about the spoons?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To completely prevent cross-contamination, creating entirely separate serving stations for restrictive diets is the safest option. Designate one clearly labeled \"Vegan/Allergen-Free\" station run by a dedicated attendant, separate from the main buffet line. Mandate that serving utensils for vegan items are never used in any other dish, and utilize serving spoons clearly marked for specific sections.",
      "source": "target",
